-- title:
--   Field-valued fibres of the fine Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation
-- statement:
--   The setting is the following. Two distinct primes $r \neq \bar r$ and a positive integer $N$ divisible by neither are fixed. The $r$-adic base consists of a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}$ which is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible element $\pi$ with respect to which $\mathcal{O}$ is adically complete, with residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal{O}$, together with a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal{O}$. Over it sits a coefficient ring $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$: a characteristic-zero domain, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, every element of $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfying some monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $v\!\det : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) is given, characterised by `hvdet`: $v\!\det(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   On the automorphic side, $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite ($0 < a$ or $0 < b$) and, by `hB`, its completion at a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$; $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it. A scheme $\mathcal{X}$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ and an assignment `pt`, sending a ring $S$, a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} S \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ and a fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure over $S$ to a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} S \to \mathcal{X}$ over $f$, is assumed to be a coarse moduli datum (`h𝒳`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on points with values in algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An integer $n \geq 3$ coprime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$ is fixed, and $M \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ with its assignment `ptF` on fake elliptic curves carrying a full level-$n$ structure is a fine moduli datum (`hM`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, and bijectivity of `ptF` on $S$-points for every ring $S$). A group $G$ acts on $M$ by $\rho$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ forming a level-twist action (`hρ`: the automorphisms lie over the base, they realise the twists of full level structures by $\chi(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n\Lambda$). A morphism $p : M \to \mathcal{X}$ over the base is compatible with the two moduli descriptions and invariant under $\rho$ (`hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ a coarse moduli datum $\mathcal{Y}_\ell \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$ for curves with extra level $\ell$ is given (`h𝒴`) together with the two degeneracy morphisms $d_0^\ell, d_1^\ell : \mathcal{Y}_\ell \to \mathcal{X}$ over the base, $d_0^\ell$ forgetting the extra level and $d_1^\ell$ recording the target of an $\ell$-level isogeny (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`, `hd₀`, `hd₁`); and two endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal{X}$ over the base realise the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on moduli points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   The quaternionic data at $\bar r$ consist of: $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`), a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$, a finite-idelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra embedding $\iota_0 : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$, a height-one prime $v$ containing $r$, and the subgroup $\tilde\Gamma$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ consisting (by `hΓt`) of those units whose image at every height-one prime $w \neq v$ lies in the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$. Families $s_\ell \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ and $sf_\ell$ in the finite-idelic units are given satisfying `hs` for each $\ell \notin\{r,\bar r\}$: the local component of $sf_\ell$ is $s_\ell \otimes 1$ at every prime not containing $r$ and is $1$ at the primes containing $r$; the diagonal idele of $\ell$ times $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ and $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise; and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$. The groups $\tilde\Gamma_\ell$ are defined by `hΓtℓ` as $\tilde\Gamma \cap s_\ell \tilde\Gamma s_\ell^{-1}$, and $\bar w$ is a unit of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\tilde\Gamma$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   Finally, $\theta_t : \tilde\Gamma \to G$ is a homomorphism, and $\Theta_f$ assigns, to each $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map
--   $$\bigl((\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}} \to_{\mathcal{O}\text{-alg}} B) \times \Omega_{K_0,\pi}(B)\bigr) \times G \longrightarrow \{\varphi : \operatorname{Spec} B \to M \mid \varphi \text{ over } \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}\},$$
--   where $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}(B)$ is the set of Deligne data over $B$: a $B$-submodule $\mathrm{line}(M) \subseteq B \otimes_{\mathcal{O}} M$ for every full $\mathcal{O}$-lattice $M$ in $K_0^2$, with invertible quotient, compatible with inclusions of lattices, equivariant for scalar homotheties, and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$. The clauses imposed on $\Theta_f$ are: `hnat`, naturality in $B$ along $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps; `hG`, that composing with $\rho(h)$ on $M$-points turns $\Theta_f(x, gh)$ into $\Theta_f(x, g)$; `hinv`, that if $\gamma \in \tilde\Gamma$ and $x'$ is obtained from $x$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ — that is, the $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$-component of $x'$ is the $\mathrm{Fr}^{-v\!\det \iota_0(\gamma)}$-twist of that of $x$, and the Deligne datum of $x'$ is the pullback of that of $x$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ — then $\Theta_f(x', \theta_t(\gamma)g) = \Theta_f(x, g)$; `het`, a formal étaleness property: along a surjective $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $B \to B_0$ whose kernel has square zero (any two elements mapping to $0$ have product $0$), every point of $M$ over $B$ lifting a point of the source over $B_0$ comes from a unique point of the source over $B$; and `hgeom`, which for every algebraically closed field $k$ over $\mathcal{O}$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent and every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi : \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}} \to k$ asserts both that every $k$-point of $M$ is of the form $\Theta_f((\psi, P), g)$, and that $\Theta_f((\psi, P), g) = \Theta_f((\psi', P'), g')$ holds if and only if there is $\gamma \in \tilde\Gamma$ with $g' = \theta_t(\gamma)g$, with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, and with $\psi'$ equal to the $\mathrm{Fr}^{-v\!\det \iota_0(\gamma)}$-twist of $\psi$ on every $y \in \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^{v\!\det \iota_0(z)}$ for all rational scalars $z \in \tilde\Gamma$ with $\theta_t(z) = 1$.
--
--   The conclusion is as follows. Let $B$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, let $x_1, x_2$ be pairs consisting of an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$, and let $g_1, g_2 \in G$ satisfy $\Theta_f(x_1, g_1) = \Theta_f(x_2, g_2)$. Then for every field $L$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : B \to L$ there exists $\gamma \in \tilde\Gamma$ such that, writing $(\psi_j^L, P_j^L)$ for the image of $x_j$ under base change along $\varphi$ (so $\psi_j^L = \varphi \circ \psi_j$ and $P_j^L$ is the Deligne datum obtained from $P_j$ by extension of scalars):
--
--   1.
--
--   $P_2^L$ is the pullback of $P_1^L$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, i.e. for every full $\mathcal{O}$-lattice $M$ in $K_0^2$ the line of $P_2^L$ at $M$ is the preimage of the line of $P_1^L$ at $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}M$ under the base-changed isomorphism induced by $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$;
--
--   2.
--
--   for every $y \in \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^{v\!\det \iota_0(z)}$ for every $z \in \tilde\Gamma$ that is a rational scalar multiple of $1$ and satisfies $\theta_t(z) = 1$, one has $\psi_2^L(y) = \bigl(\psi_1^L \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v\!\det \iota_0(\gamma)}\bigr)(y)$;
--
--   3.
--
--   $g_2 = \theta_t(\gamma)\,g_1$.
--
--   This is the injectivity half of the fine Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation in the form needed downstream: a coincidence of two $\Theta_f$-points over a $\pi$-nilpotent base is, after specialisation to any field-valued point, accounted for by a single element of the arithmetic group $\tilde\Gamma$ acting simultaneously on the Deligne datum, on the unramified coefficient map (through a Frobenius twist by the $\pi$-valuation of the determinant) and on the level label in $G$. It is the pointwise input to [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_flat_family_isPullback_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_flat_family_isPullback_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine_eq), where these three relations are spread over a flat family covering $\operatorname{Spec} B$.
